{% extends 'site/base.html.twig' %}
{% set active = 'covenant' %}

{% block title %}The Aloha Server Covenant · Aloha Directory{% endblock %}
{% block description %}The baseline every server in the Aloha Directory agrees to.{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
    <article class="prose">
        <h1>The Aloha Server Covenant</h1>
        <p class="lead">
            Every server in the directory agrees to this short baseline. It follows the Mastodon Server Covenant,
            adapted for Aloha.
        </p>

        <ol class="covenant">
            {% for key, rule in rules %}
                <li id="{{ key }}">
                    <h2>{{ rule[0] }}</h2>
                    <p>{{ rule[1] }}</p>
                </li>
            {% endfor %}
        </ol>

        <h2>What happens if a server breaks it</h2>
        <p>
            Curators look into complaints and their own findings. A server can be paused while they investigate, and the
            admin always gets a chance to respond. Delisting needs two curators, and every delisting is published on the
            <a href="/transparency/">transparency page</a> with the rule that was broken. The full steps are on the
            <a href="/criteria/#delisting">listing criteria</a> page.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes to the covenant</h2>
        <p>
            Nextcloud GmbH runs the directory in its first phase. An advisory board of five, including at least two admins
            of listed servers, reviews the policy twice a year and hears appeals. Changes are announced 30 days ahead on
            this website and in the Aloha admin settings.
        </p>
    </article>
{% endblock %}
